<title>SOUTH KOREA: LG CHEMICAL H1 NET RISES.</title>
<headline>LG CHEMICAL H1 NET RISES.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>	 (in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)				   159    vs   106</p>
<p>    Net					    12.97 vs    11.59</p>
<p>    Turnover				  2,004.8  vs 1,712.2</p>
<p>    Profit before tax			  21.79  vs   16.97</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries			    (3.3)  vs    0.11</p>
<p>Note - South Korea's LG Chemical Ltd, a member of LG Group, is a chemical company. Its profits rose thanks to an increase in chemical prices, particularly polyvinyl chloride and polyethylene, a company official said. A rise in sales of flooring materials, automobile parts and household products also helped.  --Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
